From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:39:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on the HP OmniBook 3

The OmniBook 3 14's tree carried the ThinkPad T14s compatible to get
onto this list, and its EFI variables worked that way. Give both
OmniBook 3 laptops their own entries instead. Without QSEECOM they
have no EFI variables, so an installer cannot write a boot entry.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 0c54df5..3931b07 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2323,6 +2323,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-6-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-ultra-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-x-g2q" },
+	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-3-16-bz0" },
+	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-3-oled" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-5" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-5-16-bf1xxx" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx" },
-- 
2.56.0

